PROJECT: TRIMMING PRODUCTION, INVENTORY, QUALITY CONTROL & COST MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior software architect, manufacturing ERP consultant, inventory-control specialist, production-planning engineer, database architect, and full-stack developer.

Your task is to design and implement a production-grade web application for a manufacturing company that processes moulded plastic or similar parts through trimming operations.

The application must manage:

- Molding receipts.
- Untrimmed and trimmed stock.
- Rack and sublocation management.
- Internal Production Transfer Notes (PTNs).
- In-house employees.
- In-house piece-rate vendors.
- Outsourced vendors.
- Production planning.
- Workstation scheduling.
- Shift-wise job orders.
- Printed production documents.
- Outsourced vendor job orders.
- Outward Gate Passes (OGPs).
- Inward Gate Passes (IGPs).
- Quality control.
- Rework and repeated QC inspections.
- Vendor piece-rate earnings and payments.
- Employee labour-cost allocation.
- Product costing.
- Monthly stocktaking and reconciliation.
- Barcode and QR-code scanning.
- Management dashboards and reports.

This must be a real transaction-based application, not merely a collection of forms, spreadsheets, and dashboards.

