9. PTN — PRODUCTION TRANSFER NOTE

PTN means Production Transfer Note.

Every internal stock movement must be recorded. The application must require a PTN for every internal material movement.

Examples:

- Molding to trimming store.
- Trimming store to workstation.
- Workstation to store.
- Workstation to QC.
- QC to rework.
- Rework to workstation.
- QC-approved stock to packing.
- Packing to another authorized location.

A PTN must support:

- Automatically generated sequential number.
- Transaction date and time.
- Source location.
- Destination location.
- Item.
- Quantity.
- Production stage.
- Workstation, where relevant.
- Assigned person, where relevant.
- Related work order.
- Reason for movement.
- Remarks.
- Prepared-by user.
- Approval information.
- QR code or barcode.
- Printable document.

Support multiple items on a PTN when appropriate.

A PTN must not duplicate physical stock. It transfers stock between locations or accountable stock categories.

A movement from molding to trimming store must record the receipt and destination correctly.

A movement from store to workstation must reduce available store stock and increase stock assigned to that workstation or production order.

A return must reverse the accountable movement appropriately.

Implement configurable approval rules. Routine movements may be posted by authorized users; selected movements and adjustments may require supervisor approval.

